- types
- stdlib/json
- stdlib/rex
- stdlib/lint

'  For record construction, start at bond and the helpers below
'  lain_types. Codecs and lint live in the sibling json, rex, and
'  lint modules imported above. For computed data, read view_project
'  and reference_index before the view resolver
'  in namespace.foil. The index can tell you which record holds a
'  reference; resolving the value that reference names needs a store.
'
'  There are two levels of presentation here. weft builds node trees;
'  weft_std supplies component definitions and seeds that Eden can
'  install. graph supplies policies and seeds for graph views. The
'  runtime connects those definitions to published records.

' --- maybe ---

+ maybe
  + ok_or
    ' Convert an optional value to a result, using the supplied error when absent.
    (@ v e)
    \ error=e value=maybe[v]
    ^ either[e v]
    ? value
     > (./some item) (./ok item)
     > .none (./err error)

